==English==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|over|drive|||lang=en}}. Cognate with Norwegian {{term|overdrive||to exaggerate|lang=no}} and Dutch {{term|overdrijven||to exaggerate|lang=nl}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{context|dated|lang=en}} A [[gear]], on an automobile, higher than the normal top gear.
#* {{quote-news|work=Popular Mechanics‎|page=201|date=Oct|year=1981|volume=156|number=4|passage=Cruising in '''overdrive''' at legal highway speed keeps rpm right at 1800, depending on rear-axle ratio.}}
# A state of heightened activity.
#* {{quote-book|title=The ground beneath her feet|page=78|author=[[w:Salman Rushdie|Salman Rushdie]]|year=2000|passage=It is true, though it's got nothing to do with me, that the building boom that created the Bombay of my childhood went into '''overdrive''' in the years before my birth}}

